-- title:
--   Whittaker multiplicity one passes to elements of the cyclic span
-- statement:
--   Fix a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ (a height one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$) and write $\mathbb{Q}_v$ for the $v$-adic completion, so that `LocalGL3 v` is the group $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$. Let $\psi_v$ be a continuous additive character of $\mathbb{Q}_v$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and let $W : \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ be a function which is smooth in the sense that there is a subgroup $U_v \le \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ whose underlying set is open and with $W(gk) = W(g)$ for all $k \in U_v$ and all $g$. Assume `HasWhittakerMultOne` $\psi_v$ $W$, that is: for the representation `gl3CyclicRep W` of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ by right translation on the submodule `gl3CyclicSubspace W`, the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the right translates $h \mapsto W(\,\cdot\, h)$ of $W$, the space of $\psi_v$-Whittaker functionals `gl3WhittakerFunctionalSpace` has $\mathbb{C}$-rank at most $1$. Then for every $W'$ lying in that span `gl3CyclicSubspace W`, the same holds for $W'$: the space of $\psi_v$-Whittaker functionals on the right-translation representation on the span of the right translates of $W'$ has rank at most $1$.
--
--   This is the hereditary form of local Whittaker multiplicity one for $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over $\mathbb{Q}_v$: the bound on the dimension of the space of Whittaker functionals, being a statement about the cyclic right-translation module generated by a vector, is inherited by every vector of that module. It is used in the construction of the local Whittaker data entering the cubic induction step, being cited by [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_isCubicInductionDataOn_whittakerLoc_eq_of_mem_gl3CyclicSubspace_of_isOpen`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_isCubicInductionDataOn_whittakerLoc_eq_of_mem_gl3CyclicSubspace_of_isOpen).
